8.In view of the above submissions, now the points arise for consideration in this appeal are:
(1) Whether the appellants had established the fact that the deceased rider did not possess valid driving license to drive the two wheeler?;
(2)Whether the notional income fixed by the Tribunal is proper?; and (3)Whether the multiplier method adopted by the Tribunal in respect of the rider of the two wheeler is proper?
